[2026-03-04T20:29:54.494Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U8SHgP8rJjGfXWmAFxGaC5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Todo App\n     2→\n     3→A clean, modern task management application that lets users create, organize, and track their todos.\n     4→\n     5→## Pages\n     6→\n     7→### 1. Main Todo List Page (`/`)\n     8→\n     9→The primary page of the app. Shows all todos with filtering and creation capabilities.\n    10→\n    11→#### Header\n    12→- App title \"Todo App\" displayed at the top left\n    13→- A count of incomplete todos shown (e.g., \"3 items left\")\n    14→\n    15→#### Add Todo\n    16→- A text input at the top with placeholder \"What needs to be done?\"\n    17→- Pressing Enter with non-empty text creates a new todo and clears the input\n    18→- New todos are added to the top of the list with status \"active\" (not completed)\n    19→\n    20→#### Todo List\n    21→- Each todo item displays:\n    22→  - A checkbox on the left to toggle completion\n    23→  - The todo text in the center\n    24→  - A priority badge (Low, Medium, High) shown as a colored tag\n    25→  - A due date (if set), displayed relative to today (e.g., \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\", \"Overdue\")\n    26→  - A delete button (trash icon) on the right, visible on hover\n    27→- Completed todos have strikethrough text styling and reduced opacity\n    28→- Clicking the todo text opens the Edit Todo Modal\n    29→- Checking/unchecking the checkbox toggles the completed status and persists to the database\n    30→- Clicking the delete button removes the todo after a confirmation prompt\n    31→\n    32→#### Filters\n    33→- Filter bar below the input with buttons: \"All\", \"Active\", \"Completed\"\n    34→- The currently selected filter is visually highlighted\n    35→- \"All\" shows all todos (default)\n    36→- \"Active\" shows only incomplete todos\n    37→- \"Completed\" shows only completed todos\n    38→- A \"Clear Completed\" button on the right side removes all completed todos\n    39→\n    40→#### Sorting\n    41→- A dropdown to sort by: \"Newest First\" (default), \"Oldest First\", \"Priority\", \"Due Date\"\n    42→\n    43→### 2. Edit Todo Modal\n    44→\n    45→A modal dialog that opens when clicking a todo item's text.\n    46→\n    47→#### Fields\n    48→- **Title**: Text input, pre-filled with current todo text (required)\n    49→- **Priority**: Dropdown selector with options: Low, Medium, High (default: Medium)\n    50→- **Due Date**: Date picker input (optional)\n    51→- **Notes**: Multiline textarea for additional details (optional)\n    52→\n    53→#### Actions\n    54→- \"Save\" button: Saves changes and closes the modal\n    55→- \"Cancel\" button: Discards changes and closes the modal\n    56→- Clicking outside the modal also closes it (discarding changes)\n    57→\n    58→## Data Model\n    59→\n    60→### Todo\n    61→| Field       | Type      | Description                          |\n    62→|-------------|-----------|--------------------------------------|\n    63→| id          | UUID      | Primary key                          |\n    64→| title       | TEXT      | The todo item text (required)        |\n    65→| completed   | BOOLEAN   | Whether the todo is done             |\n    66→| priority    | TEXT      | \"low\", \"medium\", or \"high\"           |\n    67→| due_date    | DATE      | Optional due date                    |\n    68→| notes       | TEXT      | Optional additional notes            |\n    69→| created_at  | TIMESTAMP | When the todo was created            |\n    70→| updated_at  | TIMESTAMP | When the todo was last modified      |\n    71→\n    72→## API Endpoints\n    73→\n    74→### `GET /.netlify/functions/todos`\n    75→Returns all todos, sorted by `created_at` descending.\n    76→\n    77→### `POST /.netlify/functions/todos`\n    78→Creates a new todo. Body: `{ title, priority?, due_date?, notes? }`\n    79→\n    80→### `PUT /.netlify/functions/todos/:id`\n    81→Updates an existing todo. Body: partial todo fields.\n    82→\n    83→### `DELETE /.netlify/functions/todos/:id`\n    84→Deletes a todo by ID.\n    85→\n    86→### `DELETE /.netlify/functions/todos?completed=true`\n    87→Deletes all completed todos (\"Clear Completed\" action).\n    88→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dq1TZiwLFixxvGpyJG1LQ2","session_id":"0c501394-3aea-49f7-985d-e5c6f42e3e50","uuid":"ce5a56ea-4643-4f08-8400-002cf29cf606"}
